WEBVTT

00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:15,280
My oncologist said that my cancer could also change from horrible and positive negative,

00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:20,000
trying to get me to do a biopsy again. I would totally agree with you. Matter of fact,

00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:29,120
I can't tell you how many people, how many women that will start with us, so they have

00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:36,160
grant, they have hormone negative, so they have triple negative breast cancer. And we test that

00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:41,440
just in our cheek, so I'm testing that they do well with a dim or something like that.

00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:49,520
So I don't believe all those pathology reports personally. So regardless of whether your cancer

00:00:49,520 --> 00:00:55,520
switches to horrible negative or horrible positive, that would just be, I think your oncologist is

00:00:55,520 --> 00:01:00,320
just concerned that they want to switch the therapy, so they want to do change a drug.

00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:07,600
So if you're on a drug slash chemotherapy with your oncologist, that's based upon

00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:20,480
you be grand positive or grand negative, then maybe testing is in order for them. But we've had

00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:26,640
we've had patients too with multiple breast lesions and biopsy, different breast lesions,

00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:32,480
and one comes back, grand, or horrible positive, and one comes back, or no negative. So

00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:38,960
so I don't always trust those pathology reports. But if you're not doing,

00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:43,200
you know, if you're not currently doing chemo, or you don't plan on doing chemo, or you're not

00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:48,400
doing any medication, what does it make a difference to them, whether you're horrible positive or negative?

00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:55,680
So that would be my concern.

